# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git on Windows (`core.autocrlf=true`) rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout.
# That is harmless for Python, but fatal for a shell script that is executed by
# name inside the Linux image: the shebang becomes `#!/bin/sh\r`, so the kernel
# looks for an interpreter literally named `/bin/sh<CR>` and the container dies
# with `exec /app/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory` -- pointing at the
# interpreter, not the missing file, which is why it reads as a phantom.
#
# Shell scripts are the only tracked files here that are executed by name, so
# they are pinned to LF in the index *and* in every working tree. The checkout
# that builds the image and the checkout CI builds from then agree byte for byte.
*.sh text eol=lf
